Public information hasn't changed since quote 1 and nothing has traded, so the fair value is still the expected sum: 7.0 (die 1) + 7.625 (die 2) + 3.67 (die 3) + 3.67 (die 4) ≈ 21.96. The settlement has a standard deviation of about 7.1.

With alpha averaging about 0.48 across the three equally likely values, adverse selection is significant. A rough check of expected edge per side shows that quoting about 8 away from fair value is near the best trade-off between noise-trader profit and informed-trader losses. The 13.9 bid and 30 ask are roughly 8 from 21.96 on each side, so I'll keep the same quote.

