Before any reveal, the expected settlement is the sum of the die means: 7.00 + 7.625 + 3.667 + 3.667 ≈ 21.96. The total's standard deviation is about 7.1. Noise traders have valuations around 22 with sd 6, and an informed trader (probability alpha, averaging about 0.48 over the prior) buys whenever value exceeds my ask and sells whenever it is below my bid.

I centred the quote on fair value and checked half-spreads. Around 8 gives the best expected profit per side, since informed-trader losses roughly offset noise-trader spread capture at narrower widths. Widths of 3 and 6 both lose money on average, and 10 is slightly worse than 8. The quote is symmetric about 22, with bid 14.0 and ask 30.0.

