**Fair value:** Card 1 is 10, so the settlement is 10 plus the sum of cards 2 and 3. The remaining 10 cards average 5.7, so the unconditional fair value is 21.4. Past trades shift this a little. The round 1 sale at 17 when the settlement was 27 suggests alpha is probably low, and the two round 2 trades roughly offset each other. My posterior mean is about 21.5.

**Quote:** Position is 0 and this is the last quote of the round, so the goal is just expected profit. Noise-trader flow favours a spread centred near 21.5. Informed flow adds adverse selection, which is largest just beyond the value thresholds. Rough calculations put the best bid just above 18 and the best ask just above 24.9, so I'll quote 18.1 and 25.0.

